<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kashf al-Mahjub</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">11th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a> · Also known as The Revelation of the Veiled, Kashf al-mahjub</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Kashf al-Mahjub, or Revelation of the Veiled, is the oldest surviving treatise on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sufism">Sufism</a> written in Persian, composed in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lahore">Lahore</a> in the eleventh century by the mystic Ali Hujwiri. It explains Sufi doctrines and practices and gives the lives of earlier saints. Hujwiri's shrine in Lahore, known as Data Darbar, remains one of the most visited in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-asia">South Asia</a>.</p></div>
